    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec asked for a derived `ownerSegment` field on owners, formatted `<TIER>_<AREA>`. I followed the existing pattern this codebase uses for derived owner attributes (like `locality`, `timezone`, `contactPreference`, `ageBand`): a `@Transient` getter on the entity, plus a schema property so the generated DTO carries the field and MapStruct auto-maps it.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added `getOwnerSegment()`:\n   - TIER = `PREMIUM` when `getMembershipLevel() >= 3`, else `STANDARD`\n   - AREA = `METRO` when `getLocality()` is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD), else `REGIONAL`\n   - It reuses the existing `REGION_POSTCODE_RANGES` map (whose keys are exactly NSW/VIC/QLD) as the \"known region\" check, and the existing derived `getMembershipLevel()`/`getLocality()` accessors.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` string property to the `Owner` schema (kept it a plain `string` like the sibling `contactPreference`/`ageBand` fields, so MapStruct auto-maps the getter without any String\u2192enum conversion concerns).\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest` (the only test class) passes \u2014 `STANDARD_METRO` for a known region and `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown one \u2014 and `./mvnw test` reports `BUILD SUCCESS` (2/2, 0 failures).",
